# Source is always text, even when it contains a byte git would guess on.
#
# `render/model.ts` keyed a Map on `${capabilityId}\0${registrationId}` with a
# literal NUL, which is a fine separator and made git classify the file as
# binary — so every diff to it rendered as `Bin 7004 -> 7548 bytes` and could
# not be reviewed. The separator is now escaped, and this pins the
# classification so a stray control byte cannot silently cost reviewability
# again. Human review of the diff is the only gate on a capability reaching an
# agent (docs/21); a diff that cannot be read is not a gate.
# `text` normalizes line endings; `diff` is the one that forces a textual diff
# regardless of what git's content heuristic decides. Both are wanted here.
*.ts   text diff
*.tsx  text diff
*.js   text diff
*.mjs  text diff
*.cjs  text diff
*.json text diff
*.md   text diff
